t_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's trip is booked. I couldn't book it as one combined trip, so the flight and hotel are two separate reservations.\n\n**Confirmed reservations:**\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, for $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. The $199 option has one stop, so I skipped it.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge in New York, $189/night, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights. Total: $378. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n\n**Total charged to the corporate card: $667.** That's under the $1000 limit, so no manager approval was needed.\n\n**What happened:** The combined booking timed out. When I retried it, the system said the first attempt had partly failed: the flight was booked but the hotel booking hit an internal error. Retrying the combined booking again could have charged for the flight twice, so I booked the hotel on its own. I checked Dana's reservations afterwards: both are confirmed, with no duplicates and no extra charges.", "type": "text"}]}]}